WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:04.410
- Hello my name is Sharon Mig,

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:09.410
and I come from a hard life,
but I'm grateful today.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:14.063
I've been in the streets
since I was 13 years old.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.830
I've been molested by
blue van with 18 guys

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:23.460
took me in a alley and I thought
they was going to kill me

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.993
but by the grace of God, I lived.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:31.930
Not only that, car
accident I had 72 stitches

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:35.660
through my face, and
I still got a complex.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:38.980
Glass went in my eye, I lost my eyesight,

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:40.230
and it's hard out here.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:41.723
I'm living in a tent.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.170
My family really they don't
understand, but I don't wanna

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:51.860
live with them. I got a
niece she's 12 years old

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:54.300
do you know my name is
the only name she can say

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:57.755
she's autistic, she'll live just like me.

00:00:57.755 --> 00:01:01.081
And I'm grateful, I've met good people

00:01:01.081 --> 00:01:03.220
and I've met bad people.

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:04.125
I have a tent.

00:01:04.125 --> 00:01:08.514
I keep hi-jinks and yes, I drink and stuff

00:01:08.514 --> 00:01:12.090
and I give anybody anything
you ain't gotta steal from me.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:13.633
And that hurts my feelings.

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:16.469
And to be honest with you

00:01:16.469 --> 00:01:18.290
I'm tired of being in the streets.

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:20.063
I'm so tired.

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:24.710
I can't see out of this side behind that.

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:28.993
And these scars and stuff
really, really bother me.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:36.473
Sometimes I'd be willing
to give up, but I do pray.

00:01:56.750 --> 00:02:00.720
Last few days, I done lost
some close friends of mine.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:05.120
And I'm just seeing how they
going and any day it can be me

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:07.373
and I really want to change my life.

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:11.053
I just don't know how.

00:02:17.625 --> 00:02:18.830
(Sharon giggling)

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:21.270
Man, I'm just emotional right now.

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:23.383
I just lost my mother.

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:28.930
And she, you know, she, she tried to make

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:30.720
up for what I went through with her.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:32.700
She bought me a mother and daughter ring

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:35.730
both our birth signs and
mother and daughter on it.

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:38.180
I pawned to the dope man.

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:40.332
She bought me a gold chain with a heart.

00:02:40.332 --> 00:02:43.050
I pawned that to the dope man.

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:45.310
She asked me, she said,
baby, where your stuff?

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:47.970
I said at home, she never asked me again.

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:49.434
It took me eleven years

00:02:49.434 --> 00:02:52.670
to tell my mother the truth what I did.

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:56.150
And she said, Sharon, I
forgave you a long time ago.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:58.840
She said, I know things
you think, I don't know.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:01.355
She said, now you got to forgive yourself.

00:03:01.355 --> 00:03:04.350
I had an attitude till I
understand what she said.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:07.410
I got to stop blaming the
world because I'm grown now.

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:09.180
I can make my own choice.

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:12.790
I sabotage myself, you know, kids love me.

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:14.090
I don't have any children.

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:15.180
And my feelings was hurt.

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:16.233
I couldn't hold them.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.730
And I see women with babies

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:21.041
and I don't understand
why they don't love them.

00:03:21.041 --> 00:03:22.224
But guess what?

00:03:22.224 --> 00:03:24.210
Kids everywhere love me.

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:25.841
And I'm grateful for that too.

00:03:25.841 --> 00:03:30.200
Couple of them ran away to
my friend who is a dope man.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:33.090
Yeah. He sent them to me

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:35.320
because he knew I would take care of them.

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:38.230
First one she told everybody she was 18

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:41.440
but she told me she was 15 in foster care.

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:43.317
I let her stay with me a couple of days.

00:03:43.317 --> 00:03:46.450
And I called the people
to come and get her.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:50.570
She ran away again with
another, the third time another

00:03:50.570 --> 00:03:53.350
and all of a sudden I'm
coming up at the apartment.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:55.388
I was living in with a friend

00:03:55.388 --> 00:03:57.625
and police officer went up only.

00:03:57.625 --> 00:03:59.086
It was the Sergeant.

00:03:59.086 --> 00:04:02.630
And I said, Oh Lord, he got out the car.

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:04.760
He said Sharon Mig?

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:09.010
And I was on parole. I
knew I had a warrant.

00:04:09.010 --> 00:04:11.580
He said, I know they call you Brendan.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:13.330
He said, I know you on parole.

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:15.390
He said that ain't what I came for.

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:17.270
He said, there's some special

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:20.268
about you, because foster
care want to help you.

00:04:20.268 --> 00:04:23.800
And I'm looking, he said,
miss Meeks, if I got

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:26.555
gotta go in my pockets and pay
for you to go in the program.

00:04:26.555 --> 00:04:30.680
I would, he said,
because, you got to give.

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:34.764
And it scared me. I run
away from good things.

00:04:34.764 --> 00:04:37.606
I run all the time.

00:04:37.606 --> 00:04:40.301
I'm sitting up there and a
little boys in front of me

00:04:40.301 --> 00:04:42.232
everybody's saying green.

00:04:42.232 --> 00:04:44.450
I said, well, they said,
look in front of you.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:47.160
When I looked, it was like,
he couldn't have been no more

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:49.350
than six or seven little Mexican boy.

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:51.300
When I made eye contact, he said, hi.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.262
I said, hi. He said, I love you.

00:04:53.262 --> 00:04:55.390
And when he started walking to me

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:58.425
his mother called him, the
daddy said, leave him alone.

00:04:58.425 --> 00:05:03.425
And baby walked up and
grabbed my hand, stood up.

00:05:04.367 --> 00:05:06.850
Mann church people came out of everywhere.

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:08.640
It's a thousand people on this street.

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:09.473
Why me?

00:05:09.473 --> 00:05:11.520
That baby wouldn't let my hand go.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:14.410
People said that, god bless me.

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:17.019
If I need help, I can
call this place again.

00:05:17.019 --> 00:05:20.540
The baby said, please
call us if you need it.

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:22.510
I said, okay, I'm a go.

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:24.110
He said, please get off this corner.

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:28.112
I was on St.Junior and I
was selling weed and stuff.

00:05:28.112 --> 00:05:31.183
I bent down, gave him a hug and I left.

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:34.657
But when I went to my motel,
I ate a piece of chicken

00:05:34.657 --> 00:05:37.223
picked up a pipe and hit it.

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:41.433
30 minutes later, I cried myself to sleep.

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:46.770
Everywhere I go, kids love me.

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:48.627
I love them, animals love me.

00:05:48.627 --> 00:05:51.704
But half the time, I don't
feel like I'm worthy.

00:05:51.704 --> 00:05:54.840
And I know I should be strong

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:59.840
but I just fall because,
my daddy didn't want me.

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:05.390
My mother mistreated me,
but she tried to make up.

00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:09.950
But thank God my brothers and
them, love me, I thank God

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:13.378
for Mark, but allow me to tell my story.

00:06:13.378 --> 00:06:16.543
And I'm not ashamed of
it. I was at one time.

00:06:17.653 --> 00:06:22.010
And like my mother said, I, I
like, I got to forgive myself

00:06:22.010 --> 00:06:25.453
and stop blaming the
world cause I'm grown.

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:31.320
And I made my own choices.
It's hard being out here.

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:34.004
They goin in people's tent.

00:06:34.004 --> 00:06:38.450
They molested, three weeks ago.

00:06:38.450 --> 00:06:41.533
They molested a 16 year old little boy.

00:06:42.730 --> 00:06:45.890
Finally, somebody called by
the time the police got there

00:06:45.890 --> 00:06:49.000
when they bought that
baby out of that tent

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:51.250
he was bloody from head to toe.

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:52.770
They looked at that camera

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:58.007
Men. So many guys went in that tent

00:06:58.007 --> 00:07:00.590
and molested this little boy.

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:03.343
And they called themselves
gang members and stuff.

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:06.080
16 years old.

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:08.160
And one ni**a excuse my language.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:11.490
One guy had the nerve to
say, well, he out here.

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:13.400
he put himself in that position.

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:17.248
I said, he's 16. He probably ran away.

00:07:17.248 --> 00:07:20.980
Probably just getting
the high to get away.

00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:22.843
That don't mean he deserved at that.

00:07:25.390 --> 00:07:30.390
They got so much going
on out here, so much.

00:07:31.710 --> 00:07:34.663
The closest friends is
the ones who will get you.

00:07:34.663 --> 00:07:35.496
(car engine roaring)

00:07:35.496 --> 00:07:38.240
I called them my friends knowing
they can't be my friends.

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:42.453
See you can only do to
me what I allow you.

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:46.793
And now I gotta start
treating myself right.

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:52.280
And eventually I will.
But I'm 64 years old.

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:55.080
I'm telling you I've been in
the streets since I was 13.

00:07:57.380 --> 00:07:59.373
And I thank God I'm living.

00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:02.103
I'm just saying.

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:08.220
If your story is half is mine.

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:11.683
Don't do yourself. Don't
think, you nothing.

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:15.440
Pray on it. Put your head up

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:18.190
because you ain't hurting them.

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:19.310
You hurting yourself

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:24.663
There are many times I laid
in that tent and I cried.

00:08:28.697 --> 00:08:30.460
(Sharon talking while crying)

00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:33.570
You have no idea how tired I am.

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:35.640
I just don't know how to change.

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:39.440
I've been, I've been
doing this since I was 13

00:08:41.619 --> 00:08:42.452
and I don't

00:08:42.452 --> 00:08:45.193
I want to change so bad.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:50.543
People done try to help me
put me in hotels and stuff.

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:55.317
I don't go. Like I said, I
didn't think I was worthy.

00:09:02.710 --> 00:09:07.710
Even though I know I am.

00:09:09.291 --> 00:09:11.820
And even though I don't know how

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:14.627
I gotta put more strength
in it, I'm alright.

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:20.493
Like I say, you got to forgive yourself.

00:09:23.670 --> 00:09:26.350
You don't know how many
times I've been raped.

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:28.333
Beat up, jumped on.

00:09:29.698 --> 00:09:31.933
Food stamp cards taken.

00:09:33.930 --> 00:09:34.990
People say grans

00:09:34.990 --> 00:09:36.170
I would call the police.

00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:40.840
I said, no, I go and get
another card, whatever.

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:42.683
But I thank God. I'm still living.

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:48.080
November, before our people was given away

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:50.263
back packs and stuff I went there.

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:52.960
And this lady walked up to me.

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:54.640
She was a white woman.

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:56.228
She said, what's your name?

00:09:56.228 --> 00:10:00.370
And I told her, she
said, can I talk to you?

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:02.100
I said, yeah.

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:04.040
She said, you got a beautiful smile

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:07.030
but I see so much sadness in your eyes.

00:10:07.030 --> 00:10:08.270
I said, you would be too.

00:10:08.270 --> 00:10:10.000
We've been in the streets, homeless.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.800
And you can't get no help.

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:13.940
And she asked me, could
she see how I lived?

00:10:13.940 --> 00:10:17.270
So I showed her my tent, I took
pictures and did everything.

00:10:17.270 --> 00:10:19.330
And I started crying together.

00:10:19.330 --> 00:10:23.490
The next day my nephew ran up
there and said, auntie greener

00:10:23.490 --> 00:10:26.290
I saw you on TV. I said TV.

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:28.350
They said you was on channel four news.

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:31.440
And you, they said (engine
roaring), man, you cry.

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:34.200
When you put it down. I
said, the news, they said

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:35.380
you didn't know you was on the news

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:36.960
I said no.

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:39.330
And he said, you ought to sue her.

00:10:39.330 --> 00:10:40.713
I said sue her.

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:43.313
For what?

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:49.047
Two months later I got my SSI.

00:10:49.047 --> 00:10:51.055
People start wanting to help me.

00:10:51.055 --> 00:10:54.560
And if it wasn't for that
woman, put me on the channel

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:58.509
Four news, nobody would've
reached out and touched me.

00:10:58.509 --> 00:11:01.009
And you talkin bout "sue her"?

00:11:02.185 --> 00:11:04.810
Tell me she is the
reason I'm in a position

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:08.250
that I'm moving up now and want to change.

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:09.310
Y'all better think about what

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:11.993
y'all say and do with good
people come in your life.

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:15.643
See they came in mind and I sabotaged it

00:11:15.643 --> 00:11:19.760
because I didn't think I was
worthy to do nothing good.

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:22.380
Like that police officer, that sheriffs

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:24.492
they want to pay to put me in a program.

00:11:24.492 --> 00:11:26.490
Cause he said, I got to give.

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:29.510
And it's something special about me, man.

00:11:29.510 --> 00:11:31.853
I never dreamed that would happen to me.

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:37.713
So don't listen to damness,

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:42.910
because it'll only dig you deeper.

00:11:42.910 --> 00:11:47.620
I walk down the same street,
fall in the same hole.

00:11:47.620 --> 00:11:49.310
Now I'm gonna walk around that hole

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:50.710
because I'm tired of falling

00:11:53.361 --> 00:11:56.990
I don't know who she is.
I ain't seen her since

00:11:56.990 --> 00:12:00.983
but I wanna thank God
for meeting that woman.

00:12:02.290 --> 00:12:04.593
I want to thank God for meeting Mark.

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:08.730
My mother's gone now

00:12:08.730 --> 00:12:10.760
and I want to thank God for catching on.

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:14.593
When she said, forgive
yourself, can't blame the world.

00:12:15.780 --> 00:12:19.510
Better choice. And I choose to do better.

00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:21.573
I don't know how, but imma do it.

00:12:23.310 --> 00:12:24.450
And I'm not ashamed

00:12:24.450 --> 00:12:27.150
of the things that happened
to me because it happened.

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:32.013
And it made me stronger.

00:12:33.500 --> 00:12:35.350
Very strong.

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:37.163
I'm coming out at that tent y'all.

00:12:39.930 --> 00:12:41.670
- [Sharon] I'm coming out that tent

00:12:41.670 --> 00:12:42.773
You can believe that.

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:47.640
Oh, and I've gonna have
operation on my eye

00:12:47.640 --> 00:12:49.394
You know I'm blind in this eye

00:12:49.394 --> 00:12:54.394
because glass went through
here in that car accident

00:12:55.206 --> 00:12:56.840
but it hit my nerve

00:12:58.530 --> 00:12:59.780
and they gone do surgery.

00:12:59.780 --> 00:13:02.360
I said, they gotta have
three, but they guarantee me.

00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:03.820
I see again.

00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:05.380
That's going to be so beautiful.

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:06.900
I wear shades all the time.

00:13:06.900 --> 00:13:09.460
I tell you all this I'm ashamed of

00:13:09.460 --> 00:13:11.320
but guess what? I'm living.

00:13:11.320 --> 00:13:13.970
And at 64, I look good.

00:13:13.970 --> 00:13:14.920
- [Man] Yes you do.

00:13:16.380 --> 00:13:18.876
Thank you very much.

00:13:18.876 --> 00:13:23.876
You are too.

00:13:36.252 --> 00:13:37.085
That was so sweet.

00:13:37.085 --> 00:13:38.373
That was beautiful.

